OL,3,GNEWSAWhy children's hospices are paying
OL,4,Ato throw away your donations
OL,5,
OL,6,FEvery week, bags of unwanted clothes,
OL,7,Fbroken toys and damaged household goods
OL,8,Fare dropped off at charity shops across
OL,9,FBritain.
OL,11,FDonors may believe they are helping a
OL,12,Fgood cause. But for many charities, a
OL,13,Fgrowing share of those donations are
OL,14,Fproving costly to process, recycle and
OL,15,Fdispose of.
OL,17,FAcorns Children's Hospice, which
OL,18,Fsupports children with life-limiting
OL,19,Fand life-threatening conditions across
OL,20,Fthe West Midlands, says it spends about
OL,21,F#100,000 a year dealing with items it
OL,22,Fcannot sell.
OL,23,APub: 14-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
